WEBVTT

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:09.619
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the 26th. Can you hear me all right? Teams is showing half of you as little grey circles.</v>

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:18.320
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, got you. Anyone actually get their weekend plans done? We were going walking, then the weather did that sideways-rain thing.</v>

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.600
<v Tomasz Nowak>I got as far as opening the back door. That was enough outdoors.</v>

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:33.500
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sensible. Oh, and the charity bake sale on Friday — apparently there was proper competition over the lemon cake. More tension than a shutdown meeting.</v>

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:45.509
<v Callum Reid>Cake's no use without coffee. That broken coffee machine in the canteen's still just an expensive flashing light. Not putting it on this meeting, before anyone says it.</v>

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:50.619
<v Fiona Doyle>Good, because I haven't got a planning code for emotional damage.</v>

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:56.200
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we disappear down that hole. Finished stuff first, then what actually needs agreeing.</v>

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:04.950
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I signed off the inspection on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit on Tuesday. That's closed, not something outstanding.</v>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:12.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I signed off the inspection on the line 1 mould temp on Tuesday as well. Both done.</v>

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:19.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. I tested the line three yesterday and it's all fine now. Nothing new coming out of that.</v>

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:29.090
<v Tomasz Nowak>Only an observation from me: saw the pressure on the newer turbine dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.909
<v Marcus Hale>Back where it was, yeah? Not still sitting low?</v>

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:39.609
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, back where it was. Just saying what I saw, not raising a job for today.</v>

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:48.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Olu, can you inspect the big valve by the gate for leaks, tomorrow at 9:30? It's urgent.</v>

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:56.609
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, I can't take that one. I'm not available for that slot, so don't put it against me.</v>

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:06.969
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Doyler, can I hand that to you instead? Inspect the big valve by the gate for leaks, tomorrow at 9:30. It's urgent.</v>

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:13.189
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll take it. The big valve by the gate, leaks, tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Doyler. That's yours rather than Olu's, then.</v>

00:02:17.969 --> 00:02:25.669
<v Marcus Hale>While we're on going out and about, I'll do a site visit at the treatment plant with the contractor today at 2pm.</v>

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Haley. Today at 2pm with the contractor, agreed.</v>

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:34.449
<v Marcus Hale>Yep. That's the visit I'm taking.</v>

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:39.629
<v Tomasz Nowak>Your sound went a bit underwater there, but I got two o'clock.</v>

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:48.930
<v Fiona Doyle>Um, I'll order spare parts for the Injection Moulding Line 3 tomorrow morning as well. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:56.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Fi, spare parts for the Injection Moulding Line 3, tomorrow morning. Not in the urgent pile.</v>

00:02:57.479 --> 00:03:03.430
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. And those aren't the parts holding up the other job, just so we don't muddle them.</v>

00:03:03.919 --> 00:03:13.020
<v Fiona Doyle>Still waiting on parts for the heater box on one, nothing we can do until they arrive. The repair's blocked; I'm not promising that for today.</v>

00:03:15.509 --> 00:03:24.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood, repair stays blocked. Separate from the repair, Fi, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the heater box on one today? It's urgent.</v>

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:31.659
<v Fiona Doyle>No, sorry, I can't take that sign-off. You'll need to hand that one to someone else.</v>

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:39.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Ash, can you take it instead? Do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the heater box on one today — it's urgent.</v>

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:47.039
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll take the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the heater box on one today. Understood on the urgency.</v>

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:55.039
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. To be clear, that's the isolation sign-off, not declaring the repair finished or releasing it to run.</v>

00:03:55.719 --> 00:03:58.169
<v Aisha Begum>Absolutely. Parts blocker hasn't magically gone away.</v>

00:03:58.719 --> 00:04:03.620
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, I'll run a function test on the line 1 TCU this afternoon.</v>

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:11.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Callum Reid. That's an 'if you've got a spare minute' one, not an urgent job.</v>

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:18.389
<v Callum Reid>Yep, low priority understood. I'll do the line 1 TCU function test this afternoon.</v>

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:26.259
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And that's separate from those inspections I said were closed. Just in case my sound chopped the names up.</v>

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.180
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, separate. Not reopening either of yours.</v>

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:33.769
<v Callum Reid>Also, I'll send the shift handover report round by the 28th.</v>

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:41.040
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Cal. Same sort of priority on that — if you've got a spare minute.</v>

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.410
<v Callum Reid>Fine, not a rush job, but by the 28th. Got it.</v>

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:55.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Olu, can you sort the training records for the new starters by the end of the week? Again, if you've got a spare minute.</v>

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:06.509
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll sort the training records for the new starters by the end of the week. I can take that, just couldn't take the valve slot.</v>

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:09.949
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, understood. Different sort of commitment.</v>

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:16.110
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. Records don't generally require me to stand outside in horizontal rain.</v>

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:24.519
<v Aisha Begum>Before we move off the people bits, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team by the 28th. That's fairly important.</v>

00:05:25.189 --> 00:05:28.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Aisha. Toolbox talk organised by the 28th, fairly important.</v>

00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:31.040
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, I'll take that.</v>

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, did you say—</v>

00:05:34.839 --> 00:05:36.939
<v Aisha Begum>The 28th. Sorry, talked over you.</v>

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:42.509
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, that's what I missed. My headset did a little robot impression.</v>

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:52.509
<v Sarah Okafor>There's also the monthly fire alarm test. Someone needs to run the monthly fire alarm test by 11am. It matters but it's not urgent. Anyone taking that?</v>

00:05:54.949 --> 00:06:00.550
<v Callum Reid>Not volunteering there, sorry. I don't want a silence to get read as me saying yes.</v>

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.699
<v Fiona Doyle>Same here, I haven't taken that one.</v>

00:06:04.509 --> 00:06:13.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. No takers, then. The monthly fire alarm test is still needed by 11am, but nobody owns it. I'm not putting a name against it.</v>

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:21.740
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, don't roll that into mine either. Mine's just the site visit at the treatment plant with the contractor today at 2pm.</v>

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood, Haley. No extras attached.</v>

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:34.509
<v Fiona Doyle>And I've got the urgent leak inspection tomorrow at 9:30, plus the spare parts order tomorrow morning, which isn't urgent. Those two are clear.</v>

00:06:35.959 --> 00:06:44.360
<v Aisha Begum>Same here — urgent lock-out tag-out sign-off today, and organising the toolbox talk by the 28th. No claim that the blocked repair is done.</v>

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:50.420
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Training records by the end of the week is clear for me.</v>

00:06:52.899 --> 00:06:57.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. And the fire alarm test remains unclaimed, not quietly agreed by the group.</v>

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.480
<v Callum Reid>Right. Back to the flashing coffee monument, then.</v>

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Enjoy the light show. Thanks, everyone, that's us.</v>
